cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software in research, please cite it as below."
title: "Censo · Evidência: full-page PDF, text sidecar and hashed manifest for content-analysis corpora (Chrome extension)"
type: software
version: 1.5.0
date-released: 2026-09-11
license: MIT
repository-code: https://github.com/fplamorim/censo-evidencia
url: https://fernandoamorim.com
authors:
  - family-names: Amorim
    given-names: Fernando Paulo Lopes
    orcid: https://orcid.org/0000-0003-1646-5366
    affiliation: "CICANT / MeLCi Lab, Universidade Lusófona, Portugal"
abstract: >-
  Local Chrome extension that captures a web page as auditable evidence for
  content-, framing- or discourse-analysis corpora: a full-page A4 PDF with an
  APA retrieval footer (date-time, URL, record ID) on every page, a TXT sidecar
  with page metadata, full text and links, SHA-256 hashes of both files, and a
  CSV manifest of the corpus. Developed with Claude Cowork (Claude Fable 5.1,
  Anthropic). No network communication.
keywords:
  - content analysis
  - corpus
  - evidence
  - reproducibility
  - political communication
  - web archiving
